W44-171 DC tree Variable-trial effort-gate perf A/B
====================================================

Date: 2026-05-21
Status: SHIPPED
Production source change: jxl-encoder/src/vardct/bitstream.rs
  + new const DC_TREE_VARIABLE_TRIAL_MIN_EFFORT = 8
  + dispatch gate at line ~2416 changed `self.effort >= 4` →
    `self.effort >= DC_TREE_VARIABLE_TRIAL_MIN_EFFORT`
  + bench-only env hook `JXL_W44_171_FORCE_TRIAL_ALL_EFFORTS` for A/B repro

Hardware: AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (32 cores), 128 GB RAM
Build: cargo build --release --features "__expert butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop parallel"
Decoder: jxl-oxide srgb_linear, fast-ssim2 (sRGB u8), butteraugli_linear (default)
Threads: 1 (single-threaded encode for fair A vs B compare; matches W44-170 protocol)
Time iters per cell: 3, best-of-N reported

Cells (14):
  PROTECT_PERF (3) — W44-171 task acceptance gates (d)/(e)/(f)/(g)/(h):
    imac_dark e5 d=1.0  (5.6 MP screenshot, the W44-170 #1 wedge)
    imac_g3   e5 d=1.0  (5.6 MP screenshot)
    codec_wiki e5 d=1.0 (4.3 MP screenshot)
  OBSERVE (6):
    terminal e5 d=1.0 (1.7 MP)
    imac_dark e5 d=2.0, d=3.0
    codec_wiki e5 d=2.0
    imac_dark/codec_wiki e7 d=1.0 (libjxl still uses kWPFixedDC at e7)
  PROTECT_E8_IDENTICAL (2) — gate boundary, must be byte-identical A vs B:
    imac_dark, codec_wiki at e8 d=1.0
  PROTECT_PHOTO (3) — photos at e5/e7 to verify no photo regression:
