    cid22_1189261 e7 d=1.0

Results — wall-time speedup (A/B, single-threaded):
  imac_dark  e5 d=1.0: 21.1× faster (15498 ms → 734 ms)
  imac_g3    e5 d=1.0: 17.6× faster (13145 ms → 747 ms)
  codec_wiki e5 d=1.0: 19.6× faster (10076 ms → 514 ms)
  terminal   e5 d=1.0: 17.4× faster (3894 ms → 224 ms)
  imac_dark  e5 d=2.0: 19.4× faster
  imac_dark  e5 d=3.0: 17.6× faster
  codec_wiki e5 d=2.0: 19.6× faster
  imac_dark  e7 d=1.0: 15.3× faster
  codec_wiki e7 d=1.0: 16.9× faster
  PROTECT_E8 cells (e8 d=1.0): 0.78× / 0.97× (essentially unchanged, gate fires for both)
  PROTECT_PHOTO cid22 e5: 18.3× / 16.5× faster (photos see the trial cost too)
  PROTECT_PHOTO cid22 e7: 12.8× faster

Results — wall ratio vs cjxl (b_ms / cjxl_ms, single-thread cjxl):
  imac_dark  e5 d=1.0: 1.10× cjxl (was 23.1× pre-W44-171 single-thread)
  imac_g3    e5 d=1.0: 1.12× cjxl
  codec_wiki e5 d=1.0: 0.99× cjxl (we BEAT cjxl single-thread)
  terminal   e5 d=1.0: 0.99× cjxl (we BEAT cjxl single-thread)
  imac_dark  e7 d=1.0: 0.88× cjxl
  codec_wiki e7 d=1.0: 0.69× cjxl

  PROTECT_E8_IDENTICAL imac_dark e8 d=1.0: 4.61× cjxl (unchanged from W44-170 baseline)
  PROTECT_E8_IDENTICAL codec_wiki e8 d=1.0: 2.68× cjxl (unchanged)

  Why e5/e6/e7 beat or match cjxl on single-thread but e8 stays >2× cjxl:
  the W44-171 fix removes the Variable-mode DC tree learn at e5-e7 (the
  78.6 % CPU hotspot on screenshots per the perf-record bisect on
  imac_dark e5 d=1.0). At e8+ our extra mechanisms (butteraugli loop,
  cfl_two_pass, EPF dynamic sharpness) take over and that's where
  remaining wall overhead lives — to be addressed by future
  W44-172+ perf chunks (per the W44-170 outlier table).

