DO NOT (future agents):
- DO NOT raise DC_TREE_VARIABLE_TRIAL_MIN_EFFORT above 8 without a
  measured corpus sweep: the W44-54 sweep TSV shows Variable wins
  ~0.4-0.5 % bytes on average at e8/e9, so disabling Variable at e8+
  would cost on those cells.
- DO NOT lower DC_TREE_VARIABLE_TRIAL_MIN_EFFORT below 8 without
  re-measuring the wall-time wedge: the W44-171 fix is libjxl-parity
  AND removes 78.6 % of CPU on the worst-case cell. Earlier gates
  re-introduce the wedge.
- DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for ANY of the byte deltas observed
  here (per W44-66 user correction). The bytes differ because we
  emit a DIFFERENT DC tree (kWPFixedDC vs Variable-learned),
  producing different ANS-encoded LfGlobal contents. The quantized
  DC coefficients themselves are identical, so decoded pixels are
  byte-for-byte identical.
- DO NOT respawn this chunk under W44-172+ thinking the
  +2.17 %/+2.22 % byte cost is a regression to fix — measurement is
  conclusive that this is the libjxl-parity cost for the kLearn
  gate. If a future zenanalyze-discriminator approach can reduce
  the cost (e.g., admit Variable only on photo-class images at e5-e7),
  that's a separate chunk with its own acceptance criteria, not a
  W44-171 follow-on.

